// MAP STRINGS - TOURISTS
"Strings.Tourists.Food.Wednesday": "Oh man, that dish smells so goood. Have you ever smelled anything so tasty?",
"Strings.Tourists.Clothing.Wednesday": "I am in love with this flower dress. I don't know when I would ever wear it, but it's so pretty that I can't look away. This has been such a cool show. Have you enjoyed it?",
"Strings.Tourists.Lupini.Wednesday": "The artist perfectly captured the aura of the Persian Lily. You can almost feel the sunset.",
"Strings.Tourists.Mom.Wednesday": "I've already purchased several plants and seeds to take home! I'll be the envy of the whole village.",
"Strings.Tourists.Kid.Wednesday": "Mooooommmmm this is *sooooo* boring. I want a Cotton Candy.",
"Strings.Tourists.Food.Thursday": "I had to come back for seconds. I'm thinking of buying a dozen to take home with me. Know what I mean?",
"Strings.Tourists.Clothing.Thursday": "I don't have much of a green thumb, but I really enjoy seeing all the beautiful flowers. Maybe I'll buy a bouquet or two to take home.",
"Strings.Tourists.Lupini.Thursday": "The more time I spend examining this painting, the more I feel I must speak with the artist about their use of color and shading. It's quite extraordinary.",
"Strings.Tourists.Mom.Thursday": "I'm really excited to see which of the bouquets wins first prize this year! I hope it's the colorful one.",
"Strings.Tourists.Kid.Thursday": "Mom, can I get a Cranberry Candy? I promise I'll be good.",

// MAP STRINGS - FLOWERS
"Strings.Flowers.WagonDisplay1": "Even old wheelbarrows can be repurposed to house plants and flowers! You'd be surprised what clever use can be made of repurposing old equipment and tools.",
"Strings.Flowers.SangriaBed": "A raised wooden garden bed full of Sangria St. John's Wort. Available for sale at the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.PaintedTongueBed": "A raised wooded garden bed brimming with bright Painted Tongue flowers. Available for sale at the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.SlippersGarden": "A raised stone garden bed displaying a collection of Darwin's Slippers in full bloom. Available to purchasee from the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.Flowerbox.Wednesday": "Freshly cut Persian Lilies, locally grown. All proceeds benefit the Ferngill Botanical Society.",
"Strings.Flowers.Flowerbox.Thursday": "Freshly cut Desert Marigolds, locally grown. All proceeds benefit the Ferngill Botanical Society.",
"Strings.Flowers.WagonDisplay2": "Vibrant summer Poppies make an excellent focal point in any display. Pair with Morning Glory or Passion Flower vines to evoke a sense of adventure and exotic beauty.",
"Strings.Flowers.PaintedTongueGarden": "A raised stone garden bed showcasing the kaleidoscopic brilliance of Painted Tongue flowers. Available for sale at the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.NasturtiumPot": "Nasturtium grows well in pots, just make sure the soil has proper drainage and deadhead any spent blooms. Available for sale at the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.GlorybowerPotFall": "A miniature Harlequin Glorybower tree makes for a unique indoor decoration. Available in two different styles at the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.DesertMarigoldPot": "Desert Marigolds will brighten any room. Available for sale at the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.DarwinsSlippersPot": "Impress your neighbors with this brilliant display of Darwin's Slippers. Place in a cool environment out of direct sunlight. Available for sale at the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.GlorybowerPotSpring": "A miniature Harlequin Glorybower tree makes for a unique indoor decoration. Available in two different styles at the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.ProteaBed": "A raised stone garden bed displaying Blushing Bride Proteas in full bloom. Available for sale at the furniture stall!",
"Strings.Flowers.Table1a": "*Platycodon grandiflorus* in purple and pink",
"Strings.Flowers.Table1b": "*Papaver rhoeas* in red",
"Strings.Flowers.Table2a": "*Crocosmia × crocosmiiflora*",
"Strings.Flowers.Table2b": "*Tulipa 'Acropolis', Darwin Hybrid*, in pink",
"Strings.Flowers.Table3a": "*Camellia japonica*, in white",
"Strings.Flowers.Table3b": "*Alcea rosea*, in pink",
"Strings.Flowers.Table4a": "*Cosmos sulphureus*, in orange and red",
"Strings.Flowers.Table4b": "*Petunia patagonica*",
"Strings.Flowers.CenterTable1.Wednesday": "Starburst Bouquet, submitted by Dr Elijah Welsh",
"Strings.Flowers.CenterTable2.Wednesday": "Cosmos Bouquet, submitted by Hattie Mondridge",
"Strings.Flowers.CenterTable1.Thursday": "Three Sisters Bouquet, submitted by Marysue St. Francis",
"Strings.Flowers.CenterTable2.Thursday": "Nebula Bouquet, submitted by Evelyn Mullner",

// MAP STRINGS - MISC
"Strings.Misc.Furniture1.Wednesday": "Handcrafted by a local artisan, this table and crystal display will be sure to spark conversation. The crystal is cut from a single Sunstone. Can you feel its warmth? Not for sale - display only. Inquiries for purchase can be made to Logo's Hodgepodge.",
"Strings.Misc.Furniture2.Wednesday": "Limited edition tea set in mint. Each set is wheel-thrown and hand painted. Not for sale - display only. Inquiries for purchase can be made to Logo's Hodgepodge.",
"Strings.Misc.Furniture3.Wednesday": "Painted by esteemed botanical artist J. Audubon III, signed and numbered. Comes with easel for easy display.",
"Strings.Misc.Furniture1.Thursday": "A hand-carved Grandfather Clock, guaranteed to last generations.",
"Strings.Misc.Furniture2.Thursday": "Handcrafted by a local artisan, this end table is the perfect size to fit into any nook. Comes with decorative book and phial! Inquiries for purchase can be made to Logo's Hodgepodge.",
"Strings.Misc.Furniture3.Thursday": "Painted by esteemed botanical artist J. Audubon III, signed and numbered. Comes with easel for easy display.",
"Strings.Misc.OpenBook": "...in the blending of different elements, the subtle transition from the fixed and formal lines of art to the shifting and irregular lines of nature, and lastly in the essential convenience and livableness of the garden, lies the fundamental secret of the old garden-magic.^^However much other factors may contribute to the total impression of charm, yet by eliminating them one after another, by *thinking away* the flowers, the sunlight, the rich tinting of time, one finds that, underlying all these, there is the deeper harmony of design...^^Edith Wharton",
"Strings.Misc.Boombox": "A soft lilting piano melody drifts out across the clearing. It reminds you of the feeling of lying in a field of wildflowers on a warm sunny day.",
"Strings.Misc.FlowerDress.Wednesday": "The design of this dress was inspired by spring Tulips. Body made of soft cotton with a light, transparent layer of glittering tulle. Handsewn replicas of Frozen Tears mimic morning dew on flower petals. For Display Only.",
"Strings.Misc.Outfit.Wednesday": "A hand-dyed silky ensemble perfect for an afternoon garden party.",
"Strings.Misc.FlowerDress.Thursday": "Hyacinth and hibiscus leaves were used to achieve the light purple color of this dress. Made from sustainably sourced silk.",
"Strings.Misc.Outfit.Thursday": "This yellow, sunshine-y duo is perfect for a picnic on a warm summer afternoon.",


